{{/*
The defects that break a claim by SUCCEEDING.

One shape: a method that answers where the claim says it must refuse.
The context arms red because their primitives judge a nil error, and a
subject that ignores the context it is handed reports none; a dropped
write reds because the partner reads the same value either side; a
declared sentinel reds because nothing reported it. Which of those a
given plant means is the defect's own clause to say, not this file's —
so one define serves all of them.

The shape is a bare `return` under named results. That is what lets this
work for any signature: each slot yields its own zero without this file
naming a type it may not be able to spell, and no sample value has to be
invented for a result whose type nothing here can construct.
*/}}
{{- define "suite.defect.answers-anyway" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				// The call arrives and nothing is done with it; the bare
				// return answers every slot's zero, which for the error
				// slot is the nil this claim forbids.
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /*
The idempotent claim's defect: the first call lands, the second refuses.

A closure over one bool rather than a counter — the claim is about the
repeat and nothing past it, and a counter would invite a reader to
wonder what the third call does.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.defect.second-call-errs" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		called := false
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				if called {
					{{ .ErrSlot }} = {{ renderExpr (external "errors" "New") }}({{ printf "%q" .RepeatMessage }})
					return
				}
				called = true
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /*
The substring the red must contain, appended where this generator can
quote the message from its declared home. Absent where the failure's
prose is authored in a body template, which has no constant to quote —
a weaker proof, said out loud rather than left to look identical.
*/ -}}
{{- /*
The modifiers every planted defect closes with, whatever shape it is.

Both are facts about the CHECK rather than about the defect, which is why
they live here and not in each variant: whether a red has to name a
reason, and whether the check demands a clock before it will admit a
subject at all. A clocked check refuses one with no OnClock, and a defect
refused for wiring reds without saying anything about the claim.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.frag.defect-reason" -}}
{{- if .NeedsClock }}.IgnoringClock(){{ end }}
{{- if .ReasonConst }}.Reasoned({{ renderExpr (external .Vocab .ReasonConst) }}){{ end }}
{{- end -}}


{{- /*
The agreement claim's defect: everything is refused.

The permissive direction cannot serve. A double that accepts everything
agrees with a validator that passed the drawn value, and the drawn value
is one a correct fixture has every reason to make valid — so the proof
would pass by accident rather than by planting anything.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.defect.refuses-always" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ctor) }}(tb, {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Option) }}(
			func{{ renderParams .AnonParams }} {{ renderReturns .NamedReturns }} {
				{{ .ErrSlot }} = {{ renderExpr (external "errors" "New") }}({{ printf "%q" .RefusalMessage }})
				return
			}))
	}){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}
